{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470542-hollow-mekhet-reflection-as-strix","id":470542,"title":"Hollow mekhet, reflection as strix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-06T18:16:05-07:00","id":470542,"title":"Hollow mekhet, reflection as strix","content":"I have a player who wants to play a hollow mekhet and I can see it as interesting especially with the complications it will cause her to need to over come. My only problem at the moment is how to get the reflection that is trying to kill her fleshed out.<br /> <br /> Current idea is a strix who looks like her while a reflection. This strix will be bound to her character and reflect her strength. So blood potency is equal to shadow potency and etc.<br /> <br /> Any other suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T18:39:28-07:00","id":470567,"title":"","content":"I suppose you could have a strix 'possess' the reflection through some aberration of their normal powers.<br /> <br /> In our game the mekhet had her reflection subverted by a demon that then took over. Rather than try and kill, it tried to corrupt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T18:55:23-07:00","id":470575,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea with the demon.<br /> <br /> Mostly just looking for some way to add mechanics to the reflection so it can be combated if (when) it comes up. A strix that grows like a changlings fetch seemed like a simple fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T19:00:20-07:00","id":470580,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, the Blood Potency to Shadow Potency should be a nice start. You might even base its banes off the hollow's, or at least things she does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T19:11:04-07:00","id":470610,"title":"","content":"Yes! That is a great point. The reflection's banes should be tied to the vampire even if in an unexpected way, reflecting a strength or something 'never' done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T19:29:14-07:00","id":470622,"title":"","content":"Considering the potential power of strix you might want to keep the range limit that reflections have. I think it was three miles, but even that can be a loose rein. Maybe one mile for every Shadow Potency? Presumably after a certain point it will be powerful enough to break its tie to her, perhaps at Shadow Potency 4 when it could just possess her? <br /> <br /> One of the first signs of the reflection in our story was when an older couple had been found dead, through natural causes, but their bodies were eaten, which brought police around. Strix need Vitae, and while they can get it through Breath Drinking, it might lead to some similar questions if people start dying of lack of oxygen while asleep. Rather than police you might get a health department investigation, in fear of a gas leak or something. But that' supposing an apartment building or similar residence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T19:38:29-07:00","id":470645,"title":"","content":"Well that's the thing, it will be a more sci-fi blended game. They will be traveling to colonize mars and a few supers snuck in (pc's) so this pc has given me a great tool to add tensio. Better too because she will be the ships lead doctor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T19:57:00-07:00","id":470681,"title":"","content":"Cool, the stakes are higher. On one hand she might be the first to be alerted when they find someone low on blood or having breathing problems. On the other, if recovering people start dying under her watch suspicious eyes might turn to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T20:15:25-07:00","id":470710,"title":"","content":"I got the impression that while the Ka hates the Mekhet it came from, it doesn't actually want to kill them because it can't exist without them. It's more like it wants to make their unlife long and miserable. I also like that relationship dynamic better, because it's a bit more complex. Your Ka will torment you in any way it can, but when your unlife is in danger, it will actually try to protect you out of a sense of self-preservation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T20:40:21-07:00","id":470728,"title":"","content":"I can weave that with this strix idea. The character will think it wants them dead but since it's existence is tied to the character it would want them alive and possibly save them like you said. It also weaves with the concept that strix claim to be the 'beast' (i believe that is ka but I'm unsure). A more complex dynamic will defiantly help a grander narrative grow so I appreciate your point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:28:40-07:00","id":470854,"title":"","content":"I don't remember the Hollow that well, but I suggest considering giving the Strix Twilight Form (that it can't reverse).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:56:17-07:00","id":470908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470542-hollow-mekhet-reflection-as-strix?p=470728#post470728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can weave that with this strix idea. The character will think it wants them dead but since it's existence is tied to the character it would want them alive and possibly save them like you said. It also weaves with the concept that strix claim to be the 'beast' (i believe that is ka but I'm unsure). A more complex dynamic will defiantly help a grander narrative grow so I appreciate your point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ka is a concept from ancient Egyptian religion. It is the counterpart to the Ba, and together they are the dual aspects that make up a person. In the broadest strokes, the Ba is the body and the Ka is the soul.<br /> <br /> The idea of the Hollow Mekhet is that their Ka and Ba were separated, leaving the Mekhet herself as an empty body, and the Ka as a disembodied spirit. Neither can exist without the other, so if either dies the other dies with it, but the Ka despises its Ba because it sees the Ba as having got the better end of the deal - the Ba can interact with the world physically, and live a more-or-less normal life, while the Ka is left as intangible, invisible, as a shadow with nothing casting it. This animosity causes the Ka to torment the Ba for revenge, but ultimately unless it becomes suicidal, it will protect the Ba if its life is threatened.<br /> <br /> This parallels perfectly with the Strix's feelings toward the Kindred, so I agree that it makes more sense to run the Ka as a modified Strix than as a modified ghost. If you want to tie in the idea of Strix as the Beast, maybe Hollow Mekhet don't frenzy? What if they make Frenzy checks normally, but when they fail, instead of going into Frenzy themselves, the Strix does? It would make the prospect a bit more appealing, as the original mechanic was almost all-downside (you are completely unable to communicate over the phone or any recorded media, and are constantly at risk of breaching the masquerade if anyone notices you don't have a shadow, reflection, or echo, and in exchange you get to be haunted by an evil spirit that looks just like you and hates your guts? What's not to love!) and gives the ST a good guideline for when to have the Ka's activities cause problems for the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:58:26-07:00","id":470909,"title":"","content":"Thank you Charlaquin for the explanation. I do very much appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T05:35:58-07:00","id":471149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470542-hollow-mekhet-reflection-as-strix?p=470908#post470908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This parallels perfectly with the Strix's feelings toward the Kindred, so I agree that it makes more sense to run the Ka as a modified Strix than as a modified ghost. If you want to tie in the idea of Strix as the Beast, maybe Hollow Mekhet don't frenzy? What if they make Frenzy checks normally, but when they fail, instead of going into Frenzy themselves, the Strix does? It would make the prospect a bit more appealing, as the original mechanic was almost all-downside (you are completely unable to communicate over the phone or any recorded media, and are constantly at risk of breaching the masquerade if anyone notices you don't have a shadow, reflection, or echo, and in exchange you get to be haunted by an evil spirit that looks just like you and hates your guts? What's not to love!) and gives the ST a good guideline for when to have the Ka's activities cause problems for the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really neat take. It would make it viable as a Merit (which it wasn't in 1e).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T12:21:03-07:00","id":483792,"title":"","content":"Not quite the same, but in my games Red Jack (from Mythologies) is a particularly powerful and cunning wandering Ka. His &quot;Ars Speculorum&quot; powers compose a particular ritual that subsumes the ka of the individual taught into Jack, making that person into an additional anchor for him (a secret price in the deal most kindred making such deals are not aware of). Thanks to this Red Jack is considerably more mobile than most such beings, having managed to accrue dozens, possibly hundreds of anchors across the Earth. And while this might make him maybe the only one of its kind possibly capable of outliving its original &quot;other half&quot;, Jack still feels an uncertainty bordering on paranoia about the subject, to the point of imprisoning the original hollow Mekhet in torpor in a &quot;safe place&quot; of his creation and choice, the Glass Mansion (Reliquary, pg. 60-63), the source of legends about Jack's &quot;realm of mirrors&quot; and another source of mobility for the mysterious being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-27-2023, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}